@baseUrl = http://localhost:8080

### 1. Log in. "@name login" lets later requests reuse the token.
# @name login
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "admin@localtest.co.zw",
  "password": "LocalTest-2026-Admin"
}

### 2. Who am I? Uses the token from request 1.
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/me
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.accessToken}}

### 3. Wrong password: 401, generic message
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "admin@localtest.co.zw",
  "password": "wrong-password"
}

### 4. Unknown email: the SAME message as request 3
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "nobody@localtest.co.zw",
  "password": "LocalTest-2026-Admin"
}

### 5. Deactivated user with the right password: 401, "deactivated"
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "former@localtest.co.zw",
  "password": "LocalTest-2026-Admin"
}

### 6. Blank fields: 400 with a list of what's wrong
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "",
  "password": ""
}

### 7. No token: 401
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/me

### 8. Tampered token (one extra letter): 401
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/me
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.accessToken}}x